# Primary Directives

## Project Focus

This is a **Machine Learning Educational Repository** that:
- Provides structured learning path from Python basics to advanced ML/NLP
- Includes hands-on Jupyter notebooks for each topic
- Covers complete ML workflow: data cleaning, EDA, feature engineering, modeling
- Offers real-world projects and assignments
- Serves as a comprehensive resource for data science learners

## Current State

- ✅ Repository structure established
- ✅ Learning modules organized (12 main modules)
- ✅ Documentation framework in place
- ✅ Quality assurance scripts implemented
- ✅ ZERO copy policy enforced
- 📝 Content development in progress

## Documentation Accuracy

- Documentation must accurately reflect the educational content
- Learning paths must be clear and progressive
- Code examples must be educational and well-explained
- No misleading descriptions of ML concepts or techniques
- All examples should be practical and relevant

## Content Maintenance

- Maintain educational focus and clarity
- Ensure progressive difficulty (beginner → intermediate → advanced)
- Keep code examples well-commented for learners
- Connect concepts to real-world applications
- Update documentation as content is added
- Follow ZERO copy policy strictly
